1
00:00:00,810 --> 00:00:10,343
Right this way, Mr. and Mrs. Stewart.

2
00:00:10,343 --> 00:00:13,300
Well, it's small, but clean.

3
00:00:13,300 --> 00:00:20,331
Clean? You call this clean?

4
00:00:20,331 --> 00:00:21,800
Have a nice stay.

5
00:00:21,800 --> 00:00:30,800
Thank you. I don't believe this.

6
00:00:30,800 --> 00:00:36,848
Well, it isn't the Watermill Inn,

7
00:00:36,848 --> 00:00:48,612
but let's get a look at the view.

8
00:00:48,612 --> 00:00:50,500
How is the view?

9
00:00:50,500 --> 00:00:55,057
Great, if you enjoy looking at a parking lot.

10
00:00:55,057 --> 00:00:59,300
Well, maybe we'll see the view in the morning.

11
00:00:59,300 --> 00:01:15,300
Right now, we should clean up this room.

12
00:01:15,300 --> 00:01:18,100
Sorry, Marilyn.

13
00:01:18,100 --> 00:01:19,700
Why should you be sorry?

14
00:01:19,700 --> 00:01:25,068
Well, the rain, the room, the view of the parking lot.

15
00:01:25,068 --> 00:01:27,905
It isn't the way I hoped it would be.

16
00:01:27,905 --> 00:01:30,500
Stop blaming yourself.

17
00:01:30,500 --> 00:01:37,600
After all, we're here, we're alone, we're together.

18
00:01:37,600 --> 00:01:42,200
And I love you. Isn't that enough?

19
00:01:42,200 --> 00:01:42,400
It is for me,

20
00:01:42,200 --> 00:01:47,007
but I wanted this weekend to be special for you.

21
00:01:47,007 --> 00:01:56,409
It is special. Happy anniversary.

22
00:01:56,409 --> 00:01:59,618
It's still raining. I want to play tennis.

23
00:01:59,618 --> 00:02:00,900
I want some breakfast.

24
00:02:00,900 --> 00:02:03,905
Let's call room service and order a nice breakfast,

25
00:02:03,905 --> 00:02:06,221
and then we'll figure out what to do today.

26
00:02:06,221 --> 00:02:14,600
Right. Would you give me room service, please?

27
00:02:14,600 --> 00:02:23,700
I beg your pardon? Oh, I see.

28
00:02:23,700 --> 00:02:27,800
They don't have room service at Old Country Inn.

29
00:02:27,800 --> 00:02:30,875
Well, let's go down to the coffee shop.

30
00:02:30,875 --> 00:02:32,800
They don't have a coffee shop.

31
00:02:32,800 --> 00:02:39,400
We can get our meals at Mrs. Montefiore's down the road.

32
00:02:39,400 --> 00:02:40,863
That's OK, honey.

33
00:02:40,863 --> 00:02:43,000
I love walking in the rain.

34
00:02:43,000 --> 00:02:46,200
Oh, you're being a really good sport about this, Marilyn,

35
00:02:46,200 --> 00:02:47,900
but I think we should face the truth.

36
00:02:47,900 --> 00:02:49,500
What's that?

37
00:02:49,500 --> 00:02:52,209
This is not the way to spend our fifth anniversary.

38
00:02:52,209 --> 00:02:56,100
Well, what do you want to do?

39
00:02:56,100 --> 00:02:57,600
Why don't we get in the car and drive home?

40
00:02:57,600 --> 00:03:01,100
Oh, Richard, it really isn't that bad.

41
00:03:01,100 --> 00:03:06,000
Do you want to stick it out for the whole weekend?

42
00:03:06,000 --> 00:03:08,000
Well, I'll admit the room is uncomfortable.

43
00:03:08,000 --> 00:03:10,242
Uh-hum.

44
00:03:10,242 --> 00:03:12,100
And I do feel bad about your mother

45
00:03:12,100 --> 00:03:14,800
having to take care of the baby all weekend.

46
00:03:14,800 --> 00:03:16,519
Why don't we just check out?

47
00:03:16,519 --> 00:03:24,000
OK.

48
00:03:24,000 --> 00:03:28,400
Hello? Yes. Yes, this is she.

49
00:03:28,400 --> 00:03:33,100
Oh, hello! How nice of you to remember us!

50
00:03:33,100 --> 00:03:36,000
Yes, my husband did call.

51
00:03:36,000 --> 00:03:41,900
You do? Really? It won't be any trouble?

52
00:03:41,900 --> 00:03:47,400
Oh, yes, I think we'd like that very much.

53
00:03:47,400 --> 00:03:55,300
Fifteen minutes! Thank you. Good-bye.

54
00:03:55,300 --> 00:03:57,200
You will never guess.

55
00:03:57,200 --> 00:04:00,300
Uh ... I give up.

56
00:04:00,300 --> 00:04:05,251
Mrs. Montefiore from the Watermill Inn.

57
00:04:05,251 --> 00:04:07,800
What is she calling about?

58
00:04:07,800 --> 00:04:09,232
They have an opening.

59
00:04:09,232 --> 00:04:10,400
Someone just checked out.

60
00:04:10,400 --> 00:04:14,579
and Mrs. Montefiore has reserved the honeymoon suite for us.

61
00:04:14,579 --> 00:04:15,202
You're kidding!

62
00:04:15,202 --> 00:04:17,000
No. Isn't it wonderful?

63
00:04:17,000 --> 00:04:19,300
It's fantastic!

64
00:04:19,300 --> 00:04:23,100
Oh. Now all it has to do is stop raining.

65
00:04:23,100 --> 00:04:26,100
Let's go.
